<chapter xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude"  xml:id="chapter-8-intro">
  <title>Week 8</title>
  <introduction><p>
  This week will just be reviewing for the exam and initial interviews -- no new topics. Exam #2 will involve 
  developing simple methods (no loops) and tracing programs involving a loop.
  Be prepared to code a problem similar to <url href="https://codingbat.com/java/Warmup-1" visual="codingbat Warmup-1">Warmup-1</url>, 
  <url href="https://codingbat.com/java/String-1" visual="codingbat String-1">String-1</url>, and 
  <url href="https://codingbat.com/java/Logic-1" visual="codingbat Logic-1">Logic-1</url>
  on paper, from scratch (including method header definitions). Practice with 
  <url href="https://codingbat.com/java/Warmup-2" visual="codingbat Warmup-1">Warmup-2</url>, 
  <url href="https://codingbat.com/java/String-2" visual="codingbat String-1">String-2</url>, and 
  <url href="https://codingbat.com/java/Logic-2" visual="codingbat Logic-1">Logic-2</url> to be 
  well prepared for other questions on the exam. </p>
  </introduction>
</chapter>

